From e0fb42cb225abac2030070229bac533796fd9fe0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 3 Jul 2026 17:10:31 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] fix(premerge): finish internal de-stage across generators,
 taxonomies, and release gate

Pre-merge is a documentation gate embedded in /ship and /review, not a numbered
stage or invokable /premerge command. Completes #269 downstream where residue
still modeled pre-merge as a stage.

- agents-config.js: AGENTS.md + Cursor generators emit the embedded pre-merge
  gate instead of a /premerge stage/command.
- plugin-catalog.js: drop STAGES.PREMERGE; changesets/release-please move to the
  ship stage. recommend.js: drop STAGE_NAMES.premerge.
  harness-capability-matrix.js: drop the orphan premerge subskills.
- release-readiness.js: widen premergeEmbeddedGateStatus to certify the de-stage
  across the generator + taxonomy surfaces; status.js uses a slash-command probe
  so the legacy AUTHORITATIVE_STAGE_NAMES.premerge name-map (kept for
  currentStage='premerge' round-trip) is tolerated.
- Regenerate the D20 bd call-site kill-list: removing STAGES.PREMERGE shifts the
  @beads/bd install line in plugin-catalog.js (102->101), and the status.js
  reconciliation comments shift its .beads/bd lines (+10). Deterministic,
  line-number-only update via the module renderer.
- Tests: flip agents-md/cursor/plugin-catalog locking assertions to the
  embedded-gate model; add release-readiness-premerge-gate certification.

Legacy round-trip preserved (status-command.test.js:190, workflow/state.test.js).
release check: success, 0 blockers.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
